v4.0.15
Radon Player 4.0.15: clips with sound, Repeats (a tab, the DJ and Wrapped), and fixes
**Install or update:** `RadonPlayer-Next.apk` (Android), `Radon-Player-4.0.15.msi` (Windows), `radon-player_4.0.15_amd64.deb` (Linux). Each installs over the version you have and keeps your settings and stats.

**What is new**
- **Share a clip with sound:** a song's Options has **Share a clip with sound…**: a short video (.mp4) of a card with the song's cover, its name and artist and a seek bar that fills as it plays, with the song itself playing, so it plays sound wherever you post it. Two sliders set where it starts and ends, from 3 seconds to a minute; if the song is playing, "Start where it's playing" and "Hear it from there" help find the spot. The card comes in every lyrics card style. Save it or share it; the phone has Instagram and Facebook buttons, and on the PC Share saves it to Downloads › Radon Player and copies the file to paste into a message. Only a song you have as a file (yours, or a download) can be clipped: a stream has no file to take the sound from.
- **Lyrics cards with sound:** the Lyrics card box has a new tick, **With the song's sound**. With it on the card is shared as a short video with the song playing, from the first line you tick to where the last one stops (no seek bar on it). It needs the song's timed lyrics and its file; without them the card is a picture as before.
- **Clips in Personalization:** Song clip style, Song clip length (15, 30, 45 or 60 seconds to begin with) and Lyrics cards with sound, after Lyrics card style.
- **Plays on cards:** lyrics cards, picture cards and song clips say how often you have played the song beside the artist ("Saint Motel · 132 plays"). Personalization › Plays on cards switches it off.
- **Repeats, a new tab:** each time a song plays to its end and starts over by itself with **Repeat one** on is counted as one repeat of it (Repeat all, and picking a song again yourself, don't count). The **Repeats** tab (Statistics in the menu) lists your songs by how often you let them play again, with each one's longest run in a row, for all time, the last year, 30 days or 7 days.
- **Repeats from before, and from other services:** nothing recorded repeats before this version, and no service says a song was on Repeat one. So the app looks through what you played here before, your Last.fm scrobbles and your imported history (Spotify, Deezer, YouTube Music, Tidal, and Apple Music's Play Activity file) for a song played again the moment it ended, and takes each for a repeat. It does this by itself after an import, when Last.fm is connected, and once after this update; what it finds is kept and not looked for again until your history changes. It is a good guess, not a record. Apple's daily counts and a library exported from the Music app have no exact times, so no repeats can be found from those; Settings says so beside the imports.
- **The DJ knows your repeats:** with the DJ on and a song on Repeat one it says so as the song starts over: at three and five times in a row, at its 10th, 25th, 50th, 100th… repeat, when a run passes the song's longest ever, and after a long run it offers to carry on with something else (the Repeats tab has a switch for that). Four new sets: **Can't let go** (your most repeated songs), **This month's obsessions**, **Old obsessions** (what you had on repeat about a year ago) and **Like your repeats** (songs close to the ones you repeat most). Before a song it may say how often you've had it on repeat, your record with it, how long since, or that its artist is the one you repeat most. With the DJ off, a milestone or a new longest run shows as a short note (a switch in the Repeats tab).
- **Repeats in Wrapped:** every Wrapped (a week, a month, a year, all time) has your repeats in it when there were any: how many and how long they add up to, your biggest obsession, your most repeated songs and artists as full lists (as long as the other lists), your longest run, your repeat day, the day of the week and time of day you repeat most, the song you repeated most each month, and the kind of repeater you are.
- **"Repeat" is now "On repeat":** the chart of what you played most lately keeps its place and is called On repeat (as the DJ calls it), so it isn't mistaken for the new Repeats tab.
- **Presets can leave your visualizers alone:** under Personalization Preset Shuffle, **Presets leave my middle visualizer** and **Presets leave my bottom visualizer**. With both on, presets bring only their looks; with one, you get a preset's other visualizer with your own. They go for presets you pick, the shuffle, presets by time of day and Follows the cover.
- **Now playing in the cover's colours:** with the Now playing look, the Now playing screen was black while every other screen took the cover's colours. It takes them now, as do the small player window, the lock-screen player and the lyrics card.
- **Jump to a letter shows:** the strip of letters down a long A to Z list never appeared. It does now, and a few names out of place (a title filed under its bracket, an accented name after Z) no longer stop it.
- **Details for support:** the line says how many problems are in it, and **Clear** empties them once they are fixed.
- **Gone:** the switch Blurred cover behind everything (Personalization › Effects). The Glass cover preset still turns the blurred cover on.
